WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.930
This is one of the biggest stories this week
and it is fascinating.

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:11.680
Donald Trump's former secretary of defense,
Jim Mattis, has completely denounced and condemned

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.230
Donald Trump.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:18.759
And predictably, Donald Trump went completely
off the deep end, exploding in an unhinged

00:00:18.759 --> 00:00:20.779
tirade last night.

00:00:20.779 --> 00:00:22.020
It's truly something.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:26.419
And I'm not aware of any time in history that
a secretary of defense has denounced the president.

00:00:26.419 --> 00:00:31.359
They served so brutally and soul so completely
and so, so wholeheartedly.

00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:35.600
I asked for other examples yesterday on Twitter
was not given any now.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.600
I want to be clear.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.650
I'm not any particular fan of Jim Mattis.

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:43.340
I'm not you know, I wasn't a big fan of Trump's
former secretary of state, Rex Tillerson.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:50.000
But it can't be denied that they were two
of the calmer voices in Trump's administration

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.390
who were even remotely connected to reality.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:56.950
Now, since leaving his position as secretary
of defense, Jim Mattis hasn't said very much

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.180
about Donald Trump.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:05.189
And he even said, I think it was about a year
ago or so roughly, that he doesn't really

00:01:05.189 --> 00:01:06.810
plan or think it's appropriate.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:11.649
I'm summarizing here to criticize the sitting
president, the president they worked for.

00:01:11.649 --> 00:01:13.090
Clearly, that has changed.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:18.460
And Jim Mattis has now denounced Trump and
accused him of ordering the military to violate

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.689
the constitutional rights of Americans.

00:01:20.689 --> 00:01:28.380
Understand that the former Trump's own former
secretary of defense is accusing Trump of

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:32.560
trying to violate the constitutional rights
of Americans.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.530
Let's look at some of Madison's letter.

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:39.170
Then we will get Trump's explosive and completely
predictable reaction.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:43.280
Mattis wrote, I have watched this week's unfolding
events angry and appalled.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.560
The words equal justice under law are carved
in the pediment of the United States Supreme

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:48.560
Court.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.840
This is precisely, precisely what protesters
are rightly demanding.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:57.029
It is a wholesome and unifying demand, one
that all of us should be able to get behind.

00:01:57.029 --> 00:02:00.280
We must not be distracted by a small number
of lawbreakers.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:04.779
The protests are defined by tens of thousands
of people of conscience who are insisting

00:02:04.779 --> 00:02:09.429
that we live up to our values, our values
as people and our values as a nation.

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:15.500
We must reject and hold accountable those
in office who would make a mockery of our

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:16.500
Constitution.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:22.420
Then Jim Mattis goes on to say in this letter,
absolutely brutally that, quote, Donald Trump

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:28.349
is the first president in my lifetime who
does not try to unite the American people,

00:02:28.349 --> 00:02:30.819
does not even pretend to try.

00:02:30.819 --> 00:02:33.120
Instead, he tries to divide us.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.890
We are witnessing the consequences of three
years of this deliberate effort.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:40.780
We are witnessing the consequences of three
years without mature leadership.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:45.500
We can unite without him drawing on the strength
inherent in our civil society.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.450
This will not be easy as the past few days
have shown.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:54.120
But we owe it to our fellow citizens, to past
generations that bled to defend our promise

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.090
and to our children.

00:02:56.090 --> 00:03:02.939
Then Mattis, who if nothing else, he chooses
his words carefully, actually references Nazis,

00:03:02.939 --> 00:03:09.319
saying, quote, Instructions given by the military
departments to our troops before the Normandy

00:03:09.319 --> 00:03:17.129
invasion reminded soldiers that the Nazi slogan
for destroying us was divide and conquer.

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:20.750
Our American answer is in union, there is
strength.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:25.959
We must summon that unity to surmount this
crisis, confident that we are better than

00:03:25.959 --> 00:03:27.409
our politics.

00:03:27.409 --> 00:03:33.580
And then lastly, talking about the Constitution,
which like him or not, and I'm no big Mattis

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:40.560
fan, he genuinely does seem to care about
the Constitution, regardless of who it is

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:46.569
that is in power, saying, quote, When I joined
the military some 50 years ago, I swore an

00:03:46.569 --> 00:03:49.400
oath to support and defend the Constitution.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:54.859
Never did I dream that troops taking that
same oath would be ordered under any circumstance

00:03:54.859 --> 00:04:01.050
to violate the constitutional rights of their
fellow citizens, much less to provide a bizarre

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:06.970
photo op for the elected commander in chief
with military leadership standing alongside,

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:13.769
referencing, of course, that horrifying photo
op earlier this week where Donald Trump gassed

00:04:13.769 --> 00:04:14.769
protest.

00:04:14.769 --> 00:04:15.769
Had protesters gassed.

00:04:15.769 --> 00:04:19.380
He didn't do it himself to clear a path to
his Bible photo op in front of St. John's

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:20.380
Church.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:25.669
I am not aware of such a brutal takedown of
a president by their own former secretary

00:04:25.669 --> 00:04:26.669
of defense.

00:04:26.669 --> 00:04:29.100
If you have an example, I am more than willing
to see it.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:34.280
Now, Trump's reaction, you have to see Trump's
reaction when the Maddis letter was published

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:35.280
yesterday.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.460
I was just waiting for Trump to go completely
crazy.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:43.250
It took a couple of hours, but he eventually
did tweeting, quote, Probably the only thing

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:49.080
Barack Obama and I have in common is that
we both had the honor of firing Jim Mattis,

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.630
the world's most overrated general.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:52.870
I asked for.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:55.729
Letter of resignation and felt great about
it.

00:04:55.729 --> 00:05:00.460
His nickname was Chaos, which I didn't like,
and change to Mad Dog.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:05.440
His primary strength was not military, but
rather personal public public relations.

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:09.229
I gave him a new life, things to do and battles
to win.

00:05:09.229 --> 00:05:11.840
But he seldom brought home the bacon.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:15.810
I didn't like his leadership style or much
else about him, and many others agree.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.340
Glad he is gone.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:23.310
Now, what's really amazing about Trump's response
is that, you know, Trump's furious.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:24.949
You can see his anger.

00:05:24.949 --> 00:05:30.720
Trump is seething that his own former secretary
of defense brutally has condemned him, but

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:35.020
he can't really come up with much to criticize
Jim Mattis with.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.560
He's an overrated general.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:38.169
And Trump said that so many times.

00:05:38.169 --> 00:05:39.789
It's a milquetoast insult.

00:05:39.789 --> 00:05:42.120
I didn't like his nickname, so I changed it.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:43.120
Who?

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.120
Who cares?

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:47.000
He was better at PR than military stuff.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:50.639
That speaks more about Trump's poor judgment
of who to hire.

00:05:50.639 --> 00:05:51.639
Right.

00:05:51.639 --> 00:05:52.639
Trump ran on.

00:05:52.639 --> 00:05:53.639
I will hire the best people.

00:05:53.639 --> 00:05:54.639
How?

00:05:54.639 --> 00:05:55.639
If this is true.

00:05:55.639 --> 00:05:59.090
If Matt Maddis is better at PR than military
stuff.

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:03.289
How did Trump stupidly hire him to run the
secretary of Defense?

00:06:03.289 --> 00:06:04.729
You don't have to like Mattis.

00:06:04.729 --> 00:06:06.680
I am no Big Jim Mattis fan.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:11.979
But if you say whose values do I prefer guiding
the country?

00:06:11.979 --> 00:06:20.169
Trump's, which are mi, mi, mi or Matisses,
which at least are ostensibly the Constitution

00:06:20.169 --> 00:06:22.550
and an appropriate interpretation of it.

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:24.509
I pick Mattis over Trump every time.

00:06:24.509 --> 00:06:26.060
Now, one more thing.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:28.760
Mattis seems to have the goods on Trump by
all estimates.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:35.310
If Jet Jim Mattis wanted to, he could actually
reveal things about Trump that may be worse

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:39.270
than anything we've seen yesterday when the
Mattis letter came out.

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:44.550
New York Times magazine's Robert Draper tweeted,
quote, Mattis is still holding back, though

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:49.759
he's privately told friends that Trump's behavior
is far worse than the reports and that the

00:06:49.759 --> 00:06:52.039
republic is on shaky footing.

00:06:52.039 --> 00:06:54.949
He knows so much more than he's currently
divulging.

00:06:54.949 --> 00:06:59.479
The reporting is a horror, a horror story.

00:06:59.479 --> 00:07:05.099
So if the truth is worse than the reporting,
as Jim Mattis reportedly said.

00:07:05.099 --> 00:07:07.539
Imagine what we don't know.

00:07:07.539 --> 00:07:11.449
Imagine what we might know in four weeks as
Donald Trump continues to unravel.

00:07:11.449 --> 00:07:15.370
Part of that unraveling appears to be Trump's
campaign.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.470
Looking at the 2020 map and panicking.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:08:17.400
And that's what I want to talk

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:29.909
about next.

